  "description": "The environmental sustainability and geography major encompasses the natural sciences, social sciences, and humanities in order to give students a broad understanding of the relationships between people, places, and the environment. Graduates of this program are prepared to understand complex human-environment and societal issues and to promote the flourishing of communities, regions, and the environment. Students choosing the geography concentration often enter careers as GIS analysts for governments or corporations, city and regional planners, or land-use planners and managers. Students choosing the geography concentration are prepared for graduate study in GIS, community development, urban planning, and public administration.",
